I walk towards the exit of the market.
I see a large flower stall.
The stall has many beautiful flowers.
I stop in front of the stall.
I look at a bundle of winter tulips.
They are very colourful.
I point at the tulips.
"How much do the tulips cost?" I ask the vendor.
The vendor holds up the tulips.
"They cost forty kroner," he answers.
"I will buy them," I say.
I pay for the flowers.
The vendor gives me the tulips.
Now I am finished at the market.
I walk back to my apartment.
I hold the colourful tulips in my hand.
I drink my hot coffee.
The sun shines over the busy market.
